Description: Extends the grammar of graphics to chromosome coordinates.
    A dimensionless karyotype layout supplies standard 'ggplot2' point,
    segment, text and track layers for markers, intervals, lines, columns,
    areas, ribbons, smoothed curves, rugs, discrete category channels, tiles,
    boxplots and violins, with physical bp/kb/Mb/Gb and genetic cM rulers.
    Complete 'ggplot' or grid objects can be anchored to genomic loci without
    entering the host scales, and native discrete position guides can draw
    chromosomes directly as the x or y axis of an ordinary 'ggplot2' chart.
    Built-in readers import chrom.sizes, FAI, BED, bedGraph, GFF3, GTF, PAF,
    SyRI and MCScanX files for local views, gene models, window summaries and
    multi-genome synteny comparisons. Compatible interactive layers can be
    viewed with the optional 'ggiraph' backend. Circular layouts retain
    base-pair sectors, radial tracks and curved connections through the same
    native layers and coordinate protocol. Results are ordinary 'ggplot'
    objects that can be themed, saved, combined with 'patchwork', 'cowplot' or
    'ggalign', or reused as components by other extensions.
    This independent refactor derives chromosome geometry and bundled example
    data from the 'RIdeogram' package by Hao et al. (2020)
    <doi:10.7717/peerj-cs.251>.
